"""
COVERED-CALL / BUY-WRITE BACKTESTER (educational, not a broker-grade simulator)
================================================================================
Backtest window: 2022-07-05 -> 2026-09-11

READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING ANY NUMBER THIS PRINTS:

1. IBKR's API does not provide historical bid/ask quotes for expired option
   contracts. There is no way to pull "what did the SPY $780 call actually
   trade at on 2023-03-03" from reqHistoricalData. So option prices in this
   backtest are NOT real historical quotes — they are Black-Scholes model
   prices, using a rolling REALIZED volatility computed from the underlying's
   own daily returns (since historical implied vol for expired chains isn't
   available either). Real option prices differ from BS-modeled prices in
   ways that matter (skew, term structure, supply/demand for that specific
   strike) — this is a real, structural limitation, not a bug to fix later.

2. Strikes are theoretical (rounded to the OTM target price), not real listed
   strike increments, because there's no historical chain to snap to.

3. Not modeled at all: commissions, slippage, bid/ask spread on fills,
   dividends (covered calls forgo dividend upside risk on assignment),
   early assignment (American-style options can be assigned before expiry —
   this only checks assignment AT simulated expiry).

4. Existing open positions are still monitored/closed even on a day the
   daily risk breaker trips — only NEW position entries are blocked that
   day. This is a deliberate, more conservative choice than the live engine
   (which halts everything, including managing what's already open).

Use this to sanity-check strategy RULES (OTM offset, take-profit/stop-loss
thresholds, position sizing), not as a promise of real-world P&L.
"""

